WEBVTT

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:03.030
It's got nothing to do with you.

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:05.090
Nothing that involves 
you, Hachiken-kun.

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:06.720
Just let people like me handle themselves.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.280
I'm fine. Don't worry about me!

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.500
Honestly, it's nothing.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.280
Let go of the reins.

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:17.370
I don't want you to suffer.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:18.580
Mikage...

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:22.110
Every single one of them...

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:25.200
Even though they're 
the ones suffering...

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:26.990
Idiots!

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.440
Don't worry about me!

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:33.260
How could I forget about 
you guys, you idiots?!

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:35.760
Drag me into it!

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.520
Kick me in the head! The stomach!

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:38.720
It's all fine by me!

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:43.220
Wait, I said no!

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:45.230
Getting involved will only hurt you!

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:47.150
I know that!

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:51.660
I'm scared about the bankruptcy 
and all the other heavy stuff!

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.490
My knees are shaking!

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:55.210
You shouldn't push yourself so hard!

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:57.560
There's nothing in it for you, and you 
can't do anything about it, either!

00:00:57.560 --> 00:00:58.940
I know that, too!

00:00:58.940 --> 00:00:59.960
Then, why?

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:02.120
I don't want to stop trying to understand!

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:08.300
I may be a complete outsider 
when it comes to agriculture...

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:11.020
I may not be able to do anything...

00:01:12.290 --> 00:01:14.170
But I can at least share the worry with you.

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:17.840
You're an only child,

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:20.920
so you've been worrying about your family 
by yourself all this time, right?

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:24.520
I know how hard it can be 
to agonize by yourself.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:27.810
That's why I didn't want this.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:30.970
You're a nice person.

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:33.450
So even if it's a heavy issue,

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.990
you would never leave us alone, right?

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:40.300
I'd kept you at arm's length 
because I knew that!

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:48.350
Because I'd make you worry and 
suffer more than you should.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:51.790
You don't have to worry so much about me!

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:52.750
I...

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:55.390
You know, it's not like I have 
specific dreams or goals.

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:56.590
So I kind of have time on my hands...

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.220
I mean, I complain a lot,

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:00.950
and talk to you about things!

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:02.550
Yeah...

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:05.040
Don't get so held up about it, okay?

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:06.600
Yeah.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:08.810
Thanks.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.330
I'll lean on you more.

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:14.380
I'll talk to you about everything.

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:16.030
Oh, yeah!

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.570
Oh, but, to be honest,

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:21.630
I'm not sure I'll be a good 
enough person to talk to since

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:23.910
I ran away from competition.

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:28.710
Stop saying you're not good enough!

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:32.880
Hachiken-kun, you're always so earnest.

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:35.730
That's the part of you that I really l—

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:44.970
Good job!

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:46.990
Go home already.

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:51.210
I'm gonna... lock the... door.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:54.980
Want me to lock the door?

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:32.490
<b>Fall Chapter Episode 9
The Last Milk</b>

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:29.300
I see.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:31.280
So Komaba's place went bankrupt

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:33.230
and Mikage's family co-signed the loan.

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:36.950
Will the Komaba Ranch be put up for auction?

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:38.410
I heard there still are some loans,

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:41.290
and the leased equipment will be removed.

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:45.220
There's really nothing you can do about this.

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:48.220
If there was an easy solution,
 they would've done it already.

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:50.720
Is your place okay, Mikage?

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:54.010
I haven't heard any details yet, 
so it's hard to say...

00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:58.780
It's likely we'll still be
 in debt when I take over.

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:02.320
Depending on how much, 
we may have to close down.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.070
Close?!

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:05.030
Icchan's said that he'll

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:08.030
work and pay back as much 
and as soon as he can,

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:11.250
but he's also said that he wants to 
send his little sisters to college.

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:14.820
I'd like to let him save 
up for that instead...

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:16.660
But does he even have a job lead?

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:20.790
<i>Why do high school students 
have to worry about loans?</i>

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:18.320
Just look at Ookawa-senpai.

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:23.490
<i>Money... It's all about money.</i>

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:27.760
<i>If there were enough money,
 no one would have to suffer.</i>

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:34.040
Money...

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:36.230
Get a grip!

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:38.850
Making money?

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:41.220
Do you have any good suggestions?

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:42.940
By which you mean...

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:45.190
Crab.

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:48.590
Cozy up to some ships run 
by the Russian mafia,

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:50.320
and take a little trip to 
their territorial waters—

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:51.720
Thank you.

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:55.790
Well if there were any low-risk 
money making schemes,

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:57.270
everyone would be doing them.

00:05:57.270 --> 00:05:58.720
Yeah.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:01.780
Even if you try to pick a cheap raw 
material and add value to it to resell

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:04.510
like with bacon and cheese, 
they need a lot of effort.

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:05.510
Yeah.

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:08.720
We're hardly at a point where we 
can think up anything worthwhile.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:11.430
Man, so powerless.

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:12.720
This is depressing.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:13.690
Come to think of it,

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:17.480
I've never thought much about 
management beyond the basics.

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:22.120
Online auction...

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:23.980
Do that and you're dead.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:25.440
<b>Girls' Dorm</b>

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:26.940
Agricultural Management 
Strategy

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:31.090
That's it!

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:31.990
Time for a break.

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:36.330
Not like I really get everything 
in there, anyway...

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:41.670
But I can share the worry with you.

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:51.510
Having money is a blessing, isn't it?

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:53.250
Where's this coming from?

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:55.070
When I decided to go to college,

00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:58.760
my parents said sure without batting an eye.

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:02.630
College isn't cheap, you know?

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:04.820
Made me realize how lucky we are.

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:07.590
You have a clear goal, 
so wouldn't you go to college,

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:10.030
even if you had to apply 
for a scholarship.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:13.740
Yeah, I probably would.

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:18.910
I'll do whatever it takes 
to get in and become a vet.

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:21.000
At least take this!

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:23.730
<i>My parents suck,</i>

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:28.210
<i>but I guess they're earning money 
so that they can send me to college.</i>

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:29.370
I quit Tokyo University.

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:33.490
Man, my idiot brother pisses me off!

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:35.350
Don't underestimate idiots!

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:42.040
What would your family do, Mikage, 
if you wanted to go to college?

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:44.170
I'm not going to college.

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:45.610
Just talking possibilities.

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:48.150
Forget being the co-signer 
for Komaba's debt, too.

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:51.860
I'm not sure how much we have in savings.

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:54.720
It depends, but if we don't have any,

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:57.410
we'd probably have to sell a couple cows.

00:07:57.800 --> 00:08:00.540
Tuition would be different between 
public and private universities, too.

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:04.930
If you did that, the Mikage Ranch's 
productivity will decrease, right?

00:08:04.930 --> 00:08:05.750
right.

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:08.970
And they might be livestock,

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:12.700
but it's not easy seeing animals you've 
take care of for so long be taken away...

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:14.390
Yeah.

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:20.180
Hello?

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:22.040
Okay.

00:08:22.930 --> 00:08:23.780
Yeah.

00:08:25.550 --> 00:08:26.860
I understand.

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:39.200
The Komaba Ranch is putting all 
of their cows on the market.

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:42.580
There's no going back now.

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:49.000
Are all of their cows are going to be sold off?

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:52.010
Yeah. Their cattle shed will be empty.

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:55.250
I'd asked them to let me know 
when it was time to buy them.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:58.470
Remember how they have a lot of old cows?

00:08:58.770 --> 00:09:01.680
I know a lot of them, so I 
thought I should see them

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:04.980
when they're being taken away...

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:06.530
I needed that.

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:11.180
<i>Even if it's tough, 
don't let go of the reins.</i>

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:12.960
Um...

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:15.610
Can I come, too?

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:18.820
I'd like to be there when the 
cows are being taken away, too.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:21.160
Is it okay if I come along?

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:26.150
Yeah, okay.

00:09:26.150 --> 00:09:27.580
I'll ask Icchan.

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:30.940
Now that that's been decided, 
I'll have to go back home today.

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:32.920
Hachiken-kun, want to stay over at our place?

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:33.640
Huh?

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:35.550
The transport truck will 
come early tomorrow morning.

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:37.150
Huh? Tomorrow morning?

00:09:37.150 --> 00:09:38.220
What about school?

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:39.120
Skip classes.

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:41.520
What? Are you talking about skipping classes?

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:44.280
I'm home.

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:45.530
Thank you for letting me stay.

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:47.110
Yo.

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:48.120
Welcome.

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:49.360
How've you been?

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:51.820
Good! Sorta...

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:54.070
Excuse me.

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:56.110
It's been a while.

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:57.290
Thank you for having me.

00:09:58.060 --> 00:09:59.410
The pay...

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:00.200
What?

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:02.620
Did you use your pay?

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:03.560
Yes!

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:05.420
When the pig I was taking care 
of at Ezonoo was butchered,

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:07.620
I bought the meat and made it into bacon.

00:10:08.780 --> 00:10:11.840
Right, that bacon was delicious!

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:14.190
We went through it really fast.

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:16.420
Yeah, it was great.

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:18.010
Thank you.

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:23.900
Although it was a bit tough my old teeth.

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:26.470
Yo, farmhand!

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:28.190
Thank you for having me!

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:30.520
I hear you're gonna go visit the Komabas?

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:31.150
Yes.

00:10:31.350 --> 00:10:32.960
You're a curious one.

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:35.380
Farms going belly-up aren't 
for show, you know.

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:36.400
Oh, Pa!

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:38.630
It's tough to see.

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:42.680
Yes, I know...

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:48.780
Well, I don't think I can say that, 
because I'm an outsider.

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:51.340
So, I don't know anything.

00:10:51.810 --> 00:10:54.810
I don't know what to do for my friend.

00:10:54.810 --> 00:10:58.760
But, I don't want to stop 
trying to understand.

00:10:59.770 --> 00:11:01.380
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:04.980
This idea is something I 
learned from Mikage... san.

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:08.480
Eat up and go to sleep already.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:09.770
It'll be an early start tomorrow.

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:11.070
I... I'll be okay!

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:12.220
I'm always up early!

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:12.760
Shuddup!

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:13.710
Don't talk back!

00:11:13.710 --> 00:11:15.370
Right! Sorry!

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:31.210
When people and livestock leave,

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:34.500
<b>Caution: 
Bears</b>

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:34.500
buildings go downhill really quickly.

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:38.100
What will happen to their cows?

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:40.880
They'll go to different buyers on the market.

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:43.990
The young'uns will go to other dairy farms,

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:48.270
and will be getting milked in 
their new cattle shed by sundown.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:51.790
The older ones... It's hard to say.

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:53.580
They may go to the slaughterhouse.

00:11:54.590 --> 00:11:56.280
Ah, here they come.

00:11:57.330 --> 00:11:59.440
The market runs on a strict schedule,

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:00.550
so they're in a hurry.

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:17.290
<b>Komaba Ranch</b>

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:24.530
Morning, Icchan.

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:25.890
Hey.

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:28.290
Hachiken, you actually came?

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:29.810
Glad to see you, too!

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:32.750
I'm telling you, there will 
be nothing fun about this!

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.480
I know that already!

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:38.100
Okay, good girl.

00:12:40.470 --> 00:12:41.580
Whoa!

00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:43.360
Quit it, Bass!

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:46.120
He thinks we're cow thieves.

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:47.490
He's a good guard dog.

00:12:47.810 --> 00:12:48.920
Stop barking!

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:50.490
Out!

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:08.040
Even though they might get 
sent to the slaughterhouse,

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:10.350
they aren't resisting much.

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:13.280
The Komabas have been taking good care

00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:15.760
of them from the time they were calves,

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:17.890
so they trust people.

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:22.530
That's the last one.

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:23.400
All right.

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:47.240
We will take things from here.

00:13:48.110 --> 00:13:49.450
Thank you for your hard work.

00:13:50.650 --> 00:13:52.420
Thank you.

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:07.550
I'm going to check out the market.

00:14:07.550 --> 00:14:08.910
Take care of the rest, okay?

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:09.530
'Kay.

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:16.370
Komaba.

00:14:17.420 --> 00:14:19.400
You just have to clean the cattle shed?

00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:20.290
I'll help.

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:22.820
You won't get paid.

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:23.960
I don't want to be!

00:14:24.470 --> 00:14:26.420
I'm gonna borrow your equipment!

00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:35.180
A dead rat!

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:37.100
Guess a cow stepped on it.

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:39.420
This is a giant rat!

00:14:39.420 --> 00:14:41.490
They don't have a cat here.

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:07.540
Buildings that house livestock get really 
cold when the animals leave, huh?

00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:08.340
Yeah.

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:15.890
Hey, both of you drink this before you go.

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:19.730
Milk?

00:15:20.170 --> 00:15:23.650
The last milk from Komaba Ranch,
 taken this morning.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:27.350
Thank you for the milk.

00:15:42.780 --> 00:15:44.530
It's delicious.

00:15:44.530 --> 00:15:46.000
Of course, idiot!

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:52.300
Of course it is, but that's
 still the greatest praise.

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:54.260
Thanks.

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:26.400
This story is a work of fiction.

00:17:27.050 --> 00:17:29.770
Icchan's going to start 
his part-time job today.

00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:32.210
Oh, he's already starting?

00:17:32.210 --> 00:17:34.070
He was proud that he got

00:17:34.070 --> 00:17:36.410
the moped license he needed 
for his job on the first try.

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:38.340
I'm glad.

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:40.330
He wasn't as down as I'd thought he might be.

00:17:40.980 --> 00:17:43.080
No, I think it's different.

00:17:43.670 --> 00:17:46.360
Because he's lost his dreams 
and he's all empty inside,

00:17:46.360 --> 00:17:50.040
he's just trying to get by, by finding 
some goal for the time being.

00:17:50.940 --> 00:17:52.270
How to put it...

00:17:52.870 --> 00:17:54.840
When I was in middle school,

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:56.240
I was so bent on living up

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:58.450
to my parents' expectations 
and getting good grades

00:17:59.080 --> 00:18:01.890
that I stopped thinking about 
what I was really learning

00:18:02.420 --> 00:18:04.350
or who I wanted to be.

00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:08.120
I was becoming empty...

00:18:09.140 --> 00:18:11.430
It's a scary feeling.

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:17.150
It's scary to stop working toward your dream.

00:18:17.350 --> 00:18:20.740
But it's even scarier to have a 
dream yet not work toward it

00:18:21.050 --> 00:18:22.700
and lie to yourself

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:27.330
for the rest of your life, telling 
yourself that was for the best.

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:31.500
Mikage, I still think you 
should do what you want to do!

00:18:32.020 --> 00:18:34.230
What's the point of being 
someone you're not?

00:18:36.610 --> 00:18:41.590
I've been trying to live up to my 
parents' expectations my whole life.

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:44.140
I'm sorry, Hachiken-kun.

00:18:44.650 --> 00:18:47.000
I might cause you trouble...

00:18:47.570 --> 00:18:50.600
but can I have a bit more of your courage?

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:55.030
Sure, drag me into it!

00:18:55.430 --> 00:18:57.720
I'll get my head stepped on with you!

00:19:00.950 --> 00:19:02.610
Gramps, I'm home.

00:19:02.610 --> 00:19:05.220
Oh, you walked home?

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:06.200
Yeah.

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:08.040
Taro-chan, I'm home.

00:19:10.410 --> 00:19:11.710
Oh, stop!

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:15.500
Aki, you really love horses.

00:19:15.760 --> 00:19:17.430
It's nothing new!

00:19:17.430 --> 00:19:20.950
But compared to you, I'm nowhere close.

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:21.730
True that.

00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:27.310
Hello.

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:29.020
Welcome, Uncle.

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:30.370
Hello.

00:19:30.370 --> 00:19:32.500
Oh, Hachiken-kun. You're here, too?

00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:34.830
I heard things have been 
rough for the Komabas.

00:19:34.830 --> 00:19:35.650
Yeah...

00:19:36.090 --> 00:19:40.030
We'll be in a tough spot, too, 
but, Aki, you gotta tough it out.

00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:43.030
Help your gramps and pa.

00:19:44.010 --> 00:19:45.380
We're going to spend the rest of the day

00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:48.430
talking about how we'll move 
forward from here with the business...

00:19:48.430 --> 00:19:50.340
What are you going to do, Hachiken-kun?

00:19:50.340 --> 00:19:53.210
It'll be boring stuff to an outsider.

00:19:53.210 --> 00:19:54.090
Oh...

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:55.860
I asked him to stay!

00:19:55.860 --> 00:19:56.920
Oh, really?

00:19:57.610 --> 00:20:00.050
Is Hachiken-kun a potential husband?

00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:01.660
I hope so.

00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:04.260
He's so responsible—he'd be great!

00:20:07.630 --> 00:20:10.760
We sold all their cows, 
but it's still not enough.

00:20:10.760 --> 00:20:13.260
I wonder if we can sell 
all their fields, too.

00:20:13.630 --> 00:20:16.800
Ms. Komaba and Ichirou both 
say they'll work, but...

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:20.000
They still need to raise the youngest kids.

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:22.400
We need a large sum of money.

00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:24.780
How much is the bill?

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:27.790
Roughly speaking, about fifteen million yen.

00:20:28.590 --> 00:20:30.710
Fifteen million yen...

00:20:30.710 --> 00:20:32.320
It's not so bad.

00:20:32.670 --> 00:20:35.330
Some farms have debts in the hundreds of millions.

00:20:35.640 --> 00:20:38.940
So, how should we go about repaying the loan?

00:20:38.940 --> 00:20:41.180
Maybe milk the cows three times a day?

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:44.300
Gramps and Granny are both 
getting along in their years.

00:20:44.580 --> 00:20:46.400
We'd need to hire help.

00:20:46.400 --> 00:20:48.170
How would we pay for them?

00:20:48.170 --> 00:20:50.020
We'll figure something out for the help.

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:53.010
Aki will be taking over once 
she finishes high school.

00:20:57.310 --> 00:20:58.690
All right, good.

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:02.070
First, we'll sell all the horses.

00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:06.240
Sell all of them?

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:07.740
You're going to stop having horses?

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:08.830
Yeah.

00:21:09.940 --> 00:21:13.120
It's just something I dabble 
in as a hobby, anyway.

00:21:13.380 --> 00:21:17.320
I'm getting old and I can't move 
around as much as I used to.

00:21:17.320 --> 00:21:19.970
It's a huge chore to take care of big horses.

00:21:20.780 --> 00:21:23.090
It's a good opportunity to give it up.

00:21:23.770 --> 00:21:25.290
Speaking of opportunity,

00:21:25.290 --> 00:21:27.470
I'll step down from being company 
president and let Goushi take over.

00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:29.110
That good, Goushi?

00:21:29.110 --> 00:21:30.410
O-Okay.

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:32.560
W-Wait, Dad. Are you serious?

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:34.990
I'm not president anymore

00:21:34.990 --> 00:21:37.010
Ask Goushi about the business.

00:21:37.430 --> 00:21:38.890
Bro...

00:21:38.890 --> 00:21:39.940
Yeah.

00:21:40.590 --> 00:21:42.080
Let's sell the horses.

00:21:42.080 --> 00:21:44.360
That will give us a good chunk of money.

00:21:47.780 --> 00:21:51.790
But see, we have horses, too, 
so I can still have fun!

00:21:55.720 --> 00:21:57.750
Are you really going to 
stop having any horses?

00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:00.620
Can you keep some for Aki?

00:22:00.620 --> 00:22:03.000
She really loves horses.

00:22:03.950 --> 00:22:04.810
Mikage,

00:22:05.430 --> 00:22:06.790
I know it's tough.

00:22:07.230 --> 00:22:08.530
But if you let this chance go,

00:22:08.530 --> 00:22:10.300
you might not be able to 
break it to them anymore.

00:22:10.840 --> 00:22:13.550
Putting it off will only 
make it harder on you!

00:22:15.750 --> 00:22:21.000
They might object, but I'll 
support you, no matter what!

00:22:23.870 --> 00:22:25.820
That's why I'm here!

00:22:34.550 --> 00:22:36.140
Dad, Mom,

00:22:36.140 --> 00:22:37.620
Grandpa, Granny,

00:22:37.620 --> 00:22:39.680
Great-Granny, Uncle...

00:22:40.280 --> 00:22:44.070
I can't carry on the Mikage Ranch.

00:22:46.550 --> 00:22:48.980
I have a dream!
